{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux","id":1389582,"title":"What would X be in the Exalted Setting? Redux","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-18T00:23:30-07:00","id":1389582,"title":"What would X be in the Exalted Setting? Redux","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/307115-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/307115-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting\"> What would X be in the Exalted Setting? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/307115-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/307115-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> on the OWoD we already have this game going on...so.. What would -Scott Pilgrim -Battosai Himura be in exalted? i mean both the type of exalted and the subclass, and what sort of charms would that character have </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> What would <br /> - Vox Machina and The Mighty Nein (Critical Role), The Bad Kids (Dimension 20: Fantasy High)<br /> - She-Ra and Catra<br /> be in Exalted? Both the type of Exalted and the subclass and what sort of charms would that character have","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T03:31:26-07:00","id":1389614,"title":"","content":"Adora and Catra are a Solar and her Lunar mate obviously","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T03:37:38-07:00","id":1389618,"title":"","content":"I get the appeal of these types of posts, and lord knows i've done them with DnD characters a ton, but it's just not a good match for Exalted. <br /> <br /> See, in Dungeons and Dragons you have to take the preset abilities in each class. What skills does Geralt have? Investigate, Medicine, Survival, Nature. What Tool Proficiencies? How many levels of Fighter/Hexblade.etc? But it doesn't work in Exalted. Grog is a Barbarian with a big axe. He has Melee, Resistance, Athletics. So does Kratos. So does everyone. Vax has Melee, Larceny, Dodge, Stealth. Percy is just History, Craft, Archery (flamepiece). <br /> <br /> Its not really hard, special, or interesting to remake characters in exalted because there's 20+ skills and you can just grab the really, really, obvious ones. Here, try the reverse- which famous character am I describing? He has: Single Point, Dodge, Athletics, some Resistance, and fights with a Reaper Daiklave (katana). Is that Kenshin, Zoro, Jin, Tanjiro, Zenitsu,Vergil Yusuke or Goemon?<br /> <br /> How many action game heroes are Melee, Dodge, Athletics, and some Resistance? Kratos, Cloud/Cecil/Squall/Tidus/Lightning, Dante, Bloodborne Hunter, Ryuji, Link, Haohmaru, <br /> <br /> Brawlers. Archers. Gunners. Beast Tamers. Rinse and repeat. It's just too much of an open ended game to make a build for your favorite game character that doesn't look like every other game character. You really get personality out of the Merits and Limit Triggers, but even then, its just whatever you say the character is like. you don't need to design around Exalted to play your favorite character, you can just do it. <br /> <br /> The only thing holding you back is how weird Sorcery is in Exalted, but even then, a reflavor or an artifact with custom Evocations will do anything you need it to. You could make a decent Harry Potter out of Thrown and reflavoring charms as spells. Cloud's materia (which is sort of already what hearthstones are), is easy enough as Sorcery Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T04:34:20-07:00","id":1389627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389614#post1389614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adora and Catra are a Solar and her Lunar mate obviously</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. Adora isn't actually Exalted, herself; the Sword of Protection is the source of all her powers - a custom Artifact, designed to empower a Solar's mortal servant. Catra is a catfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T04:59:47-07:00","id":1389634,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1047_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1047\" data-vbnamecard=\"1047\">vampire hunter D</a> totally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T05:05:38-07:00","id":1389636,"title":"","content":"Catra is defined as a manipulative, adaptable, and a survivor of harsh conditions with a clear animal motif (and in the original turned into a Cat). She's able to keep up with She Ra multiple times, making her some sort of exalt--I'd say yes Luanr.<br /> <br /> She Ra is yeah, a Solar (Dawn or Zenith, I'd say Zenith Athletics supernal). I won't comment on the sword to avoid spoilers, but I'd say the only &quot;issue&quot; with She Ra is that there's no reason for her to have a transformation sequence as a solar--that's probably a custom charm or related to spoilers regarding the sword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T05:18:37-07:00","id":1389639,"title":"","content":"Often these question is better asked as <br /> How would you make X character as Y Exalted splat <br /> Rather than<br /> What exalted splat is X character <br /> <br /> But that is my opinion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13712-illaden","name":"Illaden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13712_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T09:56:52-07:00","id":1389683,"title":"","content":"+1 to She-Ra and Catra = Solar + Lunar<br /> <br /> Powers wise, sure, it isn't a perfect fit, you might argue She-Ra is an Exigent given she gets all her powers through an artifact, and it's not clear if Catra is powerful enough to qualify as an Exalt.<br /> <br /> But narratively speaking, Adora and Catra are a flawless example of the Solar/Lunar bond. You have the reincarnated shining hero on one side, and her animalistic and more ruthless rival on the other. There's a tragic story of love, hate and rivalry between them, and both are able to get under the other's skin like nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T10:27:47-07:00","id":1389691,"title":"","content":"Though I've only seen the first season of She-Ra, I agree with Adora-as-Dawn. Since nobody's given a Caste suggestion for Catra, my suggestion is: Casteless Lunar.<br /> <br /> (When I first saw the thread's title, my immediate thought was, &quot;Mega Man X is an Orichalcum Caste Alchemical, obviously. I guess Zero is Soulsteel and Axl is Moonsilver.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T11:53:39-07:00","id":1389715,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25285_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25285\" data-vbnamecard=\"25285\">Epitome</a> once again, I totally agree. The Solar-Lunar bond can be profoundly ambivalent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T12:48:54-07:00","id":1389733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389691#post1389691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I've only seen the first season of She-Ra, I agree with Adora-as-Dawn. Since nobody's given a Caste suggestion for Catra, my suggestion is: Casteless Lunar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right.<br /> <br /> To the extent that Adora derives power from her sword, it's no different from how a Solar might gain powers from an N/A Artifact sword that transforms and empowers the user.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (When I first saw the thread's title, my immediate thought was, &quot;Mega Man X is an Orichalcum Caste Alchemical, obviously. I guess Zero is Soulsteel and Axl is Moonsilver.&quot;) </div> </div> </div>I always saw X as a Jade Caste and Zero as the Orichalcum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:10:25-07:00","id":1389748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389733#post1389733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right.<br /> <br /> To the extent that Adora derives power from her sword, it's no different from how a Solar might gain powers from an N/A Artifact sword that transforms and empowers the user.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I don't really care about the &quot;no powers without a sword&quot; distinction. When someone asks &quot;what Exalt type would X character be?&quot;, I usually assume they mean thematically and personality-wise. Catra doesn't literally shapeshift to my knowledge, but if she <i>were</i> an Exalt, she would.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I always saw X as a Jade Caste and Zero as the Orichalcum. </div> </div> </div>You might be right. I've always seen X as more of the Orichalcum because in addition to being an idealist, he's special in a way that he doesn't necessarily want to be. But that fits Jade as well.<br /> <br /> I like Zero as Soulsteel because he does what needs doing regardless of the cost or how anyone feels about it--he doesn't care much for illusions or high-minded rhetoric. Destroy evil people, back up good ones, and don't sweat the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:18:17-07:00","id":1389753,"title":"","content":"I want to play Exalted with Noelle Stevenson so bad it hurts (she was on a panel on D&amp;D experiences at FlameCon last time I went, but doesn\u2019t have a lot of experience with other systems). Based on Nimona, I am positive she\u2019s play a Lunar...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:34:38-07:00","id":1389756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389748#post1389748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't really care about the &quot;no powers without a sword&quot; distinction. When someone asks &quot;what Exalt type would X character be?&quot;, I usually assume they mean thematically and personality-wise. Catra doesn't literally shapeshift to my knowledge, but if she <i>were</i> an Exalt, she would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other Solars (including Solar derivatives, like Solar Coffee and Solar Lime) also have strong ties to Solars, also act as rivals, and can also have some kind of strange bond. The obligate reincarnation relationships that 2e tied into Solars and Lunars have a chokehold on the concepts that they have no business maintaining. Even 1e's Eternal Vow tended to focus overly much on Solars and Lunars, blotting every other possibility out of view, which is not a good thing to write into official materials full of different characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You might be right. I've always seen X as more of the Orichalcum because in addition to being an idealist, he's special in a way that he doesn't necessarily want to be. But that fits Jade as well.<br /> <br /> I like Zero as Soulsteel because he does what needs doing regardless of the cost or how anyone feels about it--he doesn't care much for illusions or high-minded rhetoric. Destroy evil people, back up good ones, and don't sweat the details. </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9OVv-J-LXQU\" data-code=\"9OVv-J-LXQU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9OVv-J-LXQU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T14:49:37-07:00","id":1389760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389756#post1389756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[clip of Zero asking what he is fighting for]</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider this quote instead:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Megaman Zero 4</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Big Bad Evil</b>: Bwahahaha! Are you even capable of it?! The Reploid Hero... Protecting Justice and Humanity! I am one of those humans you were sworn to protect! Do you have it in you to defeat me!?<br /> <br /> <b>Zero: </b><b>I never cared about justice, and I don't recall ever calling myself a hero... I have only ever fought for the people I believe in. I won't hesitate... If an enemy appears in front of me, I will destroy it!</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Also setting aside the Caste discussion, that quote is a good example of why Zero fits as an Alchemical. &quot;I have only ever fought for the people I believe in&quot; is pretty much the Alchemical ethos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 05-18-2020, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:36:23-07:00","id":1389810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389760#post1389760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;I have only ever fought for the people I believe in&quot; is pretty much the Alchemical ethos.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought their ethos was &quot;Robo-Communism, Ho!'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:42:45-07:00","id":1389814,"title":"","content":"-Overwatch characters<br /> -League of Legends characters<br /> -Naruto/Boruto characters<br /> -Bleach characters<br /> -My Hero Academia characters<br /> -Black Clover characters<br /> -<span style=\"color:#4D5156\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Aziraphale </span></span></span>and Crowley","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:45:54-07:00","id":1389815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389748#post1389748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't really care about the &quot;no powers without a sword&quot; distinction. When someone asks &quot;what Exalt type would X character be?&quot;, I usually assume they mean thematically and personality-wise. Catra doesn't literally shapeshift to my knowledge, but if she <i>were</i> an Exalt, she would.</div> </div> </div> </div>Adora being a Solar and Catra being anything BUT some kind of Solar would also fit why Shadow Weaver considered Adora fit to be a leader but considered Catra an inherent failure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You might be right. I've always seen X as more of the Orichalcum because in addition to being an idealist, he's special in a way that he doesn't necessarily want to be. But that fits Jade as well.<br /> <br /> I like Zero as Soulsteel because he does what needs doing regardless of the cost or how anyone feels about it--he doesn't care much for illusions or high-minded rhetoric. Destroy evil people, back up good ones, and don't sweat the details. </div> </div> </div>I'll die on the hill that humble, self-effacing X is a Jade Caste.<br /> <br /> But I'll admit that the pragmatic Soulsteel Caste does fit Zero better than the bombastic Orichalcum Caste. I guess Zero just wasn't as bombastic in canon as in some of the fanfics I read.<br /> <br /> Now, SIGMA is a perfect case of an Orichalcum Caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T18:52:10-07:00","id":1389818,"title":"","content":"Admittedly Catra being part of the institutition that raised her and Adora until Adora comes into her power legacy and rebels as the very thing said institution fought and propagandize against in their conquest - would point at a Solar Dynast vs her former fam/best friend/fianc\u00e9 Dynasts narrative.<br /> <br /> If you ignore the Beastfolk aspect of course because obviously the Great Houses don\u2019t marry or adopt those even when they are DBs, but that\u2019s just a setting nuance difference to handwave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 05-18-2020, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T19:21:28-07:00","id":1389823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389756#post1389756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9OVv-J-LXQU\" data-code=\"9OVv-J-LXQU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9OVv-J-LXQU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Perfect example. Zero kills enemies of the state, even when it hurts deeply. (As opposed to X in the same game, who has to justify his violence with black-and-white categories like &quot;Maverick.&quot;)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389815#post1389815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, SIGMA is a perfect case of an Orichalcum Caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dissonance makes the worst of the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":1961,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","user":"Dex Davican","date":". 05-18-2020, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T21:20:08-07:00","id":1389841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389627#post1389627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I disagree. Adora isn't actually Exalted, herself; the Sword of Protection is the source of all her powers - a custom Artifact, designed to empower a Solar's mortal servant.</div> </div> </div> </div>After watching episodes 1-6 of this final season and seeing what Adora did, I think it's clear that's wrong. Unless thete's something in the last few episodes that contradicts this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T21:21:05-07:00","id":1389842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389818#post1389818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ignore the Beastfolk aspect of course because obviously the Great Houses don\u2019t marry or adopt those even when they are DBs..</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? Why not?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T21:36:39-07:00","id":1389846,"title":"","content":"This may be OT but now I'm imagining an organization made up of Beastfolk who Exalt as Dragon Blooded","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:26:31-07:00","id":1389873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389842#post1389842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? Why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>They\u2019re closely associated with anathema thanks to countless war with Lunars and their beastfolk soldiers. It\u2019s one of the only \u201cracial\u201d prejudices of the Dynasty (that and Wyld mutants). A beastfolk DB who wants to serve the Realm can take the Razor or Coin, but no House is going to marry them in (barring a major in game plot point due to PCs\u2019 actions). Best they can hope for is to be appreciated as an interesting oddity like that Parrot-monk mentioned in \u201cthe Realm\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:27:20-07:00","id":1389874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389846#post1389846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This may be OT but now I'm imagining an organization made up of Beastfolk who Exalt as Dragon Blooded</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve been tinkering with an Outcaste group or two that exist as bloodlines among Beastfolk communities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:38:43-07:00","id":1389876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389841#post1389841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After watching episodes 1-6 of this final season and seeing what Adora did, I think it's clear that's wrong. Unless thete's something in the last few episodes that contradicts this</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah they already made it clear the previous season that She-Ra is an Etherian thing. The sword was Eternian tech to control it. I haven\u2019t seen the most recent season yet, but the Dumbo-arc coming was pretty obvious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:40:56-07:00","id":1389878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389818#post1389818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly Catra being part of the institutition that raised her and Adora until Adora comes into her power legacy and rebels as the very thing said institution fought and propagandize against in their conquest - would point at a Solar Dynast vs her former fam/best friend/fianc\u00e9 Dynasts narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's where my mind went. The Horde is a huge factor in their lives. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you ignore the Beastfolk aspect of course because obviously the Great Houses don\u2019t marry or adopt those even when they are DBs, but that\u2019s just a setting nuance difference to handwave.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see a third option. A beastfolk Dynast could be an \u200bindiscretion on behalf of the mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T23:51:30-07:00","id":1389879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389878#post1389878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's where my mind went. The Horde is a huge factor in their lives.<br /> <br /> I see a third option. A beastfolk Dynast could be an \u200bindiscretion on behalf of the mother.</div> </div> </div> </div>that\u2019s true... and would work with how horribly Catra is treated, and her desperation to prove herself! I\u2019m sold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:18:52-07:00","id":1389908,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> that works perfectly! Indiscretions do happen...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T14:45:48-07:00","id":1390068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389810#post1389810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought their ethos was &amp;quot;Robo-Communism, Ho!'</div> </div> </div> </div>*insert long rant about Autochthonian Orthodoxy\u2019s Functionalist hierarchy, and rejection of the concepts of class conflict, an ideal of equality, or workers controlling the means of production*<br /> <br /> There is I think a reference in the 2e CoCD reference to a brief Communal Revolution in Kamak\u2019s history that resulted in short lived Populat Council rather than the Tripartite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T17:59:08-07:00","id":1390130,"title":"","content":"Catra can also be argued to hit certain Infernal notes, given her history as a sufferer of oppression and abuse. So is Adora, but besides suffering differently, they handle it differently as well---Catra is immersed in it and seethes with it, and she often mirrors the same things inflicted upon her. Her tendency to manipulate, connive, and compulsively burn bridges has big Ebon Dragon energy in my view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T19:15:42-07:00","id":1390153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390130#post1390130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Catra can also be argued to hit certain Infernal notes, given her history as a sufferer of oppression and abuse. So is Adora, but besides suffering differently, they handle it differently as well---Catra is immersed in it and seethes with it, and she often mirrors the same things inflicted upon her. Her tendency to manipulate, connive, and compulsively burn bridges has big Ebon Dragon energy in my view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but (for most of the series) she serves the side that did the abusing, while Infernals are empowered to turn the system that\u2019s crushed them into craters","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T03:58:43-07:00","id":1390245,"title":"","content":"Can we all agree that the Sorceress who lives in Castle Greyskull (a pretty powerful Manse btw) is a Lunar, Eagle totem?<br /> <br /> Yeah, different show, just thought I'd find us some common ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T04:07:16-07:00","id":1390247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389874#post1389874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019ve been tinkering with an Outcaste group or two that exist as bloodlines among Beastfolk communities.</div> </div> </div> </div>careto share when you got something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T05:27:48-07:00","id":1390261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390245#post1390245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can we all agree that the Sorceress who lives in Castle Greyskull (a pretty powerful Manse btw) is a Lunar, Eagle totem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure her animal form is a falcon, not an eagle.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019d also probably peg her as a goddess or some other manner of spirit - something about the idea of a human living in isolation for such protracted periods, not doing anything of note, just waiting for the designated hero to drop by, it doesn\u2019t sit right with me.<br /> <br /> At least Lilith\u2019s sojourn into the wilderness, long as it was, it was her way of living with her grief, and she was <i>doing things</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-20-2020, 08:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-20T23:32:52-07:00","id":1390497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1389878#post1389878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's where my mind went. The Horde is a huge factor in their lives.<br /> <br /> I see a third option. A beastfolk Dynast could be an \u200bindiscretion on behalf of the mother.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Sudden Brainstorm Methodology!</b>*<br /> <br /> what if the Dynast in question was one of the Empress's own daughters. There could be a secret House out there made up of Beastfolk Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of calling it House Fauna.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *I came up with this idea and a neat charm name in the process. Not bad for 2:30 in the morning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T17:45:11-07:00","id":1390667,"title":"","content":"The Solar-Lunar bond isn\u2019t always based on romantic love. It could be best friends (with or without benefits) or even siblings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T18:26:16-07:00","id":1390673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390667#post1390667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Solar-Lunar bond isn\u2019t always based on romantic love. It could be best friends (with or without benefits) or even siblings.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're responding to my beef, it's not about the bond being limited to one type of relationship (as it's not, of course), but that among various quarreling immortals and demigods, it only happens between Solars and Lunars (again, with varying definitions of Solar), and gets special mechanical callouts, when there are many more demigods, and in 3e particularly, many more types of demigods. At a bare minimum, it's making it so that the Sidereals are even more disconnected from other Exalted than they should be, given how they would have known an awful lot of other Exalted before all of the skullduggery and murder of said Exalted. Even Arcane Fate can't explain that from the Sidereal end, and Lunars don't really line up as counterparts of Solars in any reasonable sense; the dark to the Solars' light is taken up by Abyssals, and Solars without restraint are Infernals. Lunars are thematically set up to contrast way more to Sidereals and particularly to Alchemicals than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T19:17:51-07:00","id":1390682,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> I was actually talking about Adora and Catra, but that\u2019s interesting. I never really thought about it that way before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T19:58:32-07:00","id":1390690,"title":"","content":"The sun and moon often have a certain resonance between them in myths. Many times whatever force governs the sun and moon are siblings or lovers (or both, ew). <br /> <br /> Also, there\u2019s a Charm to allow for a Dragon-Blooded effectively to gain that same level of bond from a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Also also, it\u2019s a weird, wide, wild world out there. Just because something isn\u2019t codified in the canon doesn\u2019t mean it can\u2019t happen at your table. Not having what Zen-Mu is <i>like</i> in a book doesn\u2019t mean you can\u2019t have Zen-Mu feature in one of your stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-22-2020, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T21:26:34-07:00","id":1390698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390673#post1390673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're responding to my beef, it's not about the bond being limited to one type of relationship (as it's not, of course), but that among various quarreling immortals and demigods, it only happens between Solars and Lunars (again, with varying definitions of Solar), and gets special mechanical callouts, when there are many more demigods, and in 3e particularly, many more types of demigods. At a bare minimum, it's making it so that the Sidereals are even more disconnected from other Exalted than they should be, given how they would have known an awful lot of other Exalted before all of the skullduggery and murder of said Exalted. Even Arcane Fate can't explain that from the Sidereal end, and Lunars don't really line up as counterparts of Solars in any reasonable sense; the dark to the Solars' light is taken up by Abyssals, and Solars without restraint are Infernals. Lunars are thematically set up to contrast way more to Sidereals and particularly to Alchemicals than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, Solars naturally contrast against Abyssals and Infernals in different ways.<br /> <br /> But how would they contrast against Lunars if NOT for the Bond?<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, it makes sense that the Sidereal Exalted are set apart and disconnected. That's practically their entire story. The absence of any Bond enforces that as much as the existence of Arcane Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-21T22:31:23-07:00","id":1390706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390673#post1390673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you're responding to my beef, it's not about the bond being limited to one type of relationship (as it's not, of course), but that among various quarreling immortals and demigods, it only happens between Solars and Lunars (again, with varying definitions of Solar), and gets special mechanical callouts, when there are many more demigods, and in 3e particularly, many more types of demigods. At a bare minimum, it's making it so that the Sidereals are even more disconnected from other Exalted than they should be, given how they would have known an awful lot of other Exalted before all of the skullduggery and murder of said Exalted. Even Arcane Fate can't explain that from the Sidereal end, and Lunars don't really line up as counterparts of Solars in any reasonable sense; the dark to the Solars' light is taken up by Abyssals, and Solars without restraint are Infernals. Lunars are thematically set up to contrast way more to Sidereals and particularly to Alchemicals than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me the Bond expresses how Solars and Lunars complete each other, not how different they are. A Solar and a Abyssal/Infernal may contrast more clearly but they do so by clashing, not by completing each other.<br /> <br /> Solar/Abyssal/Infernal is about what the Exalt is willing to do, what their goals are. Solar/Lunar is about what the Exalt <i>can</i> do. The Specialist vs the Generalist. The Most Human Exalt vs the one in touch with their Monstrous Side. The single-minded champion vs the watchful guardian taking care of everything else.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I 100% support spreading the Bond all over the place and I'm very happy Heirs has opened the Bond to DBs. I just disagree that Lunars don't line up as counterparts of Solars in any reasonable sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T02:24:48-07:00","id":1390736,"title":"","content":"So how would you do the Greek gods as exalts?<br /> <br /> What about the Sumerian ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T13:09:24-07:00","id":1390836,"title":"","content":"Olympian (mostly) Solars:<br /> <br /> Zeus as a Zenith to get that Divine Mantle action so he can be Panhelenes, worshipped by all Greeks. Also, a Dawn probably wouldn't have gotten wrecked so hard by Typhon the first time around.<br /> Aphrodite is a Dawn that gets distracted by shipping couples all the time (she's an adaptation of Innana-Ishtar and was worshipped in Sparta as Aphrodite Areia, so I'm perfectly in line to suggest this).<br /> Ares is a Dawn that tried for the battle hydra thing, got really unbalanced, and ended up venerated positively only by Sparta. No one else appreciates his commitment to maxing out all of the classic Dawn Abilities, to the detriment of Awareness, Dodge, and Resistance.<br /> Athena is a Night, because she is big on trickery.<br /> Haephestos is a Twilight.<br /> Poseidon is an Eclipse, and so is Hades. The former is the Sail and Ride part, while the latter is the reasonable liasion of the living and dead.<br /> Persephone leapt into the Underworld so hard that she became a Midnight.<br /> Dionysius is a Liminal. He has that whole death and rebirth thing going on, and in some versions, Apollo puts his heart into a mortal woman to be birthed anew after Titans tear him to pieces.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390690#post1390690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sun and moon often have a certain resonance between them in myths. Many times whatever force governs the sun and moon are siblings or lovers (or both, ew).</div> </div> </div> </div>But in Exalted, it's incredibly forced and there aren't really that many connections shared between the two. Luna isn't a moon god that runs alongside this sun like that; she's straight out of Werewolf and paired most prominently with Gaia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, there\u2019s a Charm to allow for a Dragon-Blooded effectively to gain that same level of bond from a Lunar. </div> </div> </div>Yes. It probably won't be put front and center into the setting, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also also, it\u2019s a weird, wide, wild world out there. Just because something isn\u2019t codified in the canon doesn\u2019t mean it can\u2019t happen at your table. Not having what Zen-Mu is <i>like</i> in a book doesn\u2019t mean you can\u2019t have Zen-Mu feature in one of your stories. </div> </div> </div>But if Zen-Mu were in books, it would be in danger of glutting attention like Infernals did in late 2e and hogging the camera. Or, again, as the Solar Bond does now for anything involving them and Solars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T13:38:05-07:00","id":1390844,"title":"","content":"Tbh, I thought Lunar fits better for Zeus because he's always turning into animals to seduce women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T14:42:29-07:00","id":1390852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390844#post1390844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tbh, I thought Lunar fits better for Zeus because he's always turning into animals to seduce women.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes he also turns into inanimate objects, though (&quot;a shower of gold&quot;), so you have to shop around for a different shapeshifting capacity (a la Divine Mantle). Also, none of his half-mortal progeny shapeshift, instead just being vanilla demigods with superior basic capabilities.<br /> <br /> Io arguably fits as a Lunar if you go with the story where Hera turns her into a cow, though, what with Hera being a moon goddess and all (one of a set of three given the name Selene or Luna, depending on if you're Greco or more Roman).<br /> <br /> Edit: And Hekate, as the &quot;Rotting Goddess&quot;, is a Daybreak. (drops mic)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 05-22-2020, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T14:50:20-07:00","id":1390857,"title":"","content":"The Animorphs are so lunar it hurts.<br /> <br /> They are shapeshifting heroes.<br /> They fight a guerilla war against a massively more powerful empire.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T14:55:43-07:00","id":1390859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390852#post1390852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes he also turns into inanimate objects, though (&quot;a shower of gold&quot;), so you have to shop around for a different shapeshifting capacity (a la Divine Mantle). Also, none of his half-mortal progeny shapeshift, instead just being vanilla demigods with superior basic capabilities.<br /> <br /> Io arguably fits as a Lunar if you go with the story where Hera turns her into a cow, though, what with Hera being a moon goddess and all (one of a set of three given the name Selene or Luna, depending on if you're Greco or more Roman).<br /> <br /> Edit: And Hekate, as the &quot;Rotting Goddess&quot;, is a Daybreak. (drops mic)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hekata is a Abyssal because of underworld connections and curses--with necromancy being very good at curses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T17:42:24-07:00","id":1390880,"title":"","content":"There's no explicit, canonical X-Factor in the world of Remnant to explain the chasm of difference between Huntsmen and professional soldiers.*<br /> <br /> Exaltation could easily be that X-Factor. Terrestrial Exaltation in particular, since the most notable Huntsmen are part of warrior lineages.<br /> <br /> Special lineages like Schnees and Silver-Eyed Warriors might be represented through the Divine Heritage merit and Eclipse-OK Charms.<br /> <br /> As expected, the Fire Aspect would be the most well-represented in the Huntsman community, to the point that it might be simpler to list the Huntsmen who aren't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * The best answer seems to be &quot;receiving a proper education at combat schools and Huntsman academies, showing sufficient devotion to one's training, and having enough money for a really sweet weapon&quot;, but Jaune arrived with only the devotion and a lot of raw talent, both of which allowed Pyrrha to turn him into something passable.<br /> <br /> If it's possible for Jaune to have &quot;a lot&quot; of Aura, one supposes it is possible that most people on Remnant have so little Aura that even years of rigorous combat training cannot let them attain the level of &quot;Huntsmen&quot;. Else everyone who becomes a soldier graduated from a normal high school, only trained in bootcamp, and fully intends to spend the minimum of four years in uniform before quitting.<br /> <br /> Jaune himself seems perfectly situation for a Solar Exaltation story, but the way he develops fits more the idea that he was already Exalted as an Earth Aspect, like his forefathers before him. His father merely denied him the training previous generations received.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T02:16:33-07:00","id":1390934,"title":"","content":"So...what would Horde Prime be?<br /> <br /> His arrogance and narcissism makes him seem like a First Age Solar, though the wide ranging power he weilds, and a spoilerific ability he has, seems more 2nd or even 3rd Circle Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T02:51:46-07:00","id":1390936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390934#post1390934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...what would Horde Prime be?<br /> <br /> His arrogance and narcissism makes him seem like a First Age Solar, though the wide ranging power he weilds, and a spoilerific ability he has, seems more 2nd or even 3rd Circle Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div>He\u2019s an Infernal stacked with SWLiHN themed Hive-Mind Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T12:39:28-07:00","id":1391022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390852#post1390852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sometimes he also turns into inanimate objects, though (&amp;quot;a shower of gold&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />, so you have to shop around for a different shapeshifting capacity (a la Divine Mantle). Also, none of his half-mortal progeny shapeshift, instead just being vanilla demigods with superior basic capabilities.<br /> <br /> Io arguably fits as a Lunar if you go with the story where Hera turns her into a cow, though, what with Hera being a moon goddess and all (one of a set of three given the name Selene or Luna, depending on if you're Greco or more Roman).<br /> <br /> Edit: And Hekate, as the &amp;quot;Rotting Goddess&amp;quot;, is a Daybreak. (drops mic)</div> </div> </div> </div>Helen of Troy and her siblings were hatched instead of born.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T13:16:55-07:00","id":1391031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1391022#post1391022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Helen of Troy and her siblings were hatched instead of born.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still doesn't change Zeus turning into things that aren't even animals - or even alive - to impregnate women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T04:11:04-07:00","id":1393389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390880#post1390880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jaune himself seems perfectly situation for a Solar Exaltation story, but the way he develops fits more the idea that he was already Exalted as an Earth Aspect, like his forefathers before him. His father merely denied him the training previous generations received.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counter-argument: He's the Brigid of Zeniths. Not actually good at what he wants to be (fighting), but amazing at something unique (Team Leading). Ruby isn't really a great leader, she's just got trust with her team (maybe that's changed, I stopped watching in the Atlas arc), but Jaune is a great Joan of Arc type. Zenith with bad melee stats, Presence, Medicine, 2 melee charms, War, and like 5 ox bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T08:46:19-07:00","id":1393439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1393389#post1393389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counter-argument: He's the Brigid of Zeniths. Not actually good at what he wants to be (fighting), but amazing at something unique (Team Leading). Ruby isn't really a great leader, she's just got trust with her team (maybe that's changed, I stopped watching in the Atlas arc), but Jaune is a great Joan of Arc type. Zenith with bad melee stats, Presence, Medicine, 2 melee charms, War, and like 5 ox bodies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That has some potential.<br /> <br /> If they were both Solars, I think both Jaune and Ruby would be Zeniths, but very different kinds of Zenith.<br /> <br /> <br /> What's trickiest about Zenith Jaune is his Supernal Ability. His Semblance most closely matches Solar Lore Charms, but Jaune's canonical grasp of his world's lore is infamously bad. Though I think Jaune's Lore should actually be much better, and at one point he did manage both his homework and Cardin's, and apparently did a good enough job that Doctor Oobleck didn't catch him or couldn't prove it.<br /> <br /> If not Lore, the next best candidate is Solar Presence, with its ally-buffing Charms, but Jaune isn't very persuasive or intimidating. Solar War Charms in Third Edition do absolutely nothing for assisting the efforts of a small group of named heroes. Maybe Integrity.<br /> <br /> I do favor the idea of Lore Supernal Jaune, as he responded to his father's refusal to train him to fight by instead learning as much about his &quot;Aura and Semblance&quot; as possible, with the plan to catch up on combat skills once he faked his way into Beacon behind his father's back.<br /> <br /> As for Favored Abilities, his only non-combat Favored Ability would probably be Larceny. For faking his way into Beacon and planning the heist to steal an Atlesian military aircraft.<br /> <br /> Aside from that, he could, would, and should favor Awareness, Athletics, Dodge, and Melee, because what else is he going to Favor? So holding him back in this area should require that his combat Abilities are lowly-rated and most of his Charms come from his non-combat Abilities.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as for Ruby Rose? Same Caste, but a very different story, and one that I solved years ago.<br /> <br /> <b>Caste:</b> Zenith<br /> <br /> <b>Anima Banner:</b> Her Zenith Caste Mark is a brilliant golden circle, shining like the noonday sun on her brow. Her anima banner is a bonfire of bright white and majestic gold. Her iconic display is a great crimson rose eternally shedding petals; her lesser displays of Essence are often marked by scattering red petals, particularly when she uses the Charms of her Supernal Athletics Ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Supernal Ability:</b> Athletics<br /> <br /> <b>Other Caste Abilities:</b> Integrity, Lore, Survival, and War<br /> <br /> <b>Favored Abilities:</b> Craft, Dodge, Firearms, Melee, Occult<br /> <br /> Obviously, Ruby Rose\u2019s Supernal Ability is Athletics, enabling her to learn Charms that echo her Semblance (if the story is set in Creation) or enhance her Semblance (if the story is \u201can Exaltation found its way to Remnant\u201d).<br /> <br /> Integrity reflects Ruby\u2019s unyielding core of optimism and idealism. She will make the word a better place, or die trying.<br /> <br /> Craft, Lore, and Occult represent the craftsmanship, science and mathematics, and supernatural understanding necessary to design, create, and repair Artifacts like Crescent Rose.<br /> <br /> Survival reflects how Ruby\u2019s trailers always show her wandering through the wilderness on her own; Little Red Riding Hood, out in the woods with all the Big Bad Wolves. Patch Island seems to be pretty rustic, or at least the cabin where Ruby grew up. I also imagine that Taiyang took his little girls on hunting trips to personally supervise their first encounters with the Grimm, to make sure that they were really ready. Finally, there\u2019s Ruby\u2019s connection with Zwei \u2013 he\u2019s not quite her familiar or dedicated battle-pet, but they work together easily, Ruby giving instructions and Zwei faithfully obeying.<br /> <br /> War reflects Ruby\u2019s leadership abilities, though there are no printed Charms for coordinating the efforts of a few fellow superheroes like her Huntress teammates. But if Ruby ever needed to whip a bunch of normal people into shape and lead them into battle, she would have the talent.<br /> <br /> Ruby does not favor Martial Arts, because that is not reflected in how helpless she is without her weapon; the most appropriate Style for her to learn, White Reaper Style, can be performed bare-handed. Beginning to learn that Style is on her player\u2019s To-Do List.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 06-01-2020, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T13:18:58-07:00","id":1393501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1390934#post1390934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So...what would Horde Prime be?<br /> <br /> His arrogance and narcissism makes him seem like a First Age Solar, though the wide ranging power he weilds, and a spoilerific ability he has, seems more 2nd or even 3rd Circle Demon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd go with the Demon route or a fae route to be honest. I'd make him a She Who Lives in Her Name 2nd circle, his army first circles of 2 types, maybe 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing 