"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T15:51:42-07:00","id":1393539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1393523#post1393523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Super-Dragon Blooded.<br /> <br /> Their legions must inherit their power from their Primarchs, so the Primarchs must each carry the blood of the dragons even if they're actually some other form of Exalted.<br /> <br /> A Primarch's power does not reincarnate upon death like a Celestial Exaltation, so I posit that each Primarch is a Terrestrial Exalt with awe-inspiring endowments granted via the Emperor's sorcerous workings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like their legions not being their descendants under cuts it. Leman should at least be a Lunar, Magnus maybe an Infernal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T18:15:40-07:00","id":1393561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1393539#post1393539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like their legions not being their descendants under cuts it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Their legions undergo extensive surgery and sorcerous workings to become hereditary descendants of their Primarch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Leman should at least be a Lunar, Magnus maybe an Infernal. </div> </div> </div>I'd say that Magnus is an Akuma.<br /> <br /> Leman could be a beastman to some degree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-01T23:09:44-07:00","id":1393583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1393502#post1393502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 18 Primarchs?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not gonna try to shoehorn in all their backstory lore, im just gonna stick to supernals and abilities. Its important to remember that each of them is E5 with War, Melee, Dodge. Resistance complete or near complete. That actually makes them pretty same-y, because their differences come from their personalities not their skills. <br /> <br /> Horus- Dawn War extraordinare. Took Akumazation for an extra 300xp and spent it on wyld mutations and op minmax sorcery/artifacts. <br /> <br /> Rowboat- Bureaucracy Zenith who claims to be a War Zenith. Tried to get his gf to play but she wanted to roll Fair Folk. Took Backing 5 and Resources 5. <br /> <br /> Corvus- Night Stealth. Wonders why no one else is a night stealth. <br /> <br /> Ferrus- Twilight Craft. Made an artifact out of Malfean Brass and deeply regrets being famous for it. <br /> <br /> Vulkan- Twilight Craft- specced for making artifacts. Took the brawl grapple line and the survival handle animals line. Took mighty thews twice even though thats not how it works. <br /> <br /> Perty- Twilight Craft. Specialty in Siege. Hates that Ferrus and Vulkan are crafters too so took all of resistance and said &quot;IM FINE!&quot; when asked if he still wanted to play. Has dropped from Command 5 to Command 4 about 11 times. <br /> <br /> Golden Hawk Boi- Zenith Presence. Because he's perfect. <br /> <br /> Lorgar- Zenith Performance (oratory). Calls out the ST on hypocrisy and bullshit, gets punished for it. Also the only player to use Social Combat to auto win battles but gets mocked for it. <br /> <br /> Magnus- Twilight Occult. Sorcerer. Wishes his control spell was Infallible Messenger. <br /> <br /> Jagatai: Dawn Ride. Just here to kick ass in fights, doesnt get why everyone else is such a drama lama. Surprised to be the only player invested in Integrity. <br /> <br /> Lemon Rust- Dawn Melee. Wanted to be a Lunar before the book came out, but doesn't like all the shapeshifting so he's just a heavy motiffed Solar. Has a Read Intentions roll of -2. Insists that Sorcery is demonic but his army has sorcerers so he claims its leyline magic and therefore doesnt count. <br /> <br /> Fulgrim- somehow took Appearance as a supernal? <br /> <br /> Mortarion- Resistance Dawn. Took all the cool poison resistance stuff thinking it would be useful. It wasn't. <br /> <br /> Konrad- Night Socialize, surprisingly. Took the persona line of charms work and tried to make social attacks on a mass scale work but they didnt. <br /> <br /> I Am Alpharius- Eclipse ????. Gave all his men the Giant merit. Has Dual Magus Prana and the Socialize persona death charm. <br /> <br /> Lion- exists. Dawn Melee but doesnt have a gimmick and left the table early. Half his men botched a really important Integrity roll. <br /> <br /> Angron: made a cool Spartacus/Alexander build but got upset that everyone else did basically the same so he took a homebrew soulsteel artifact with terrible, terrible drawbacks. <br /> <br /> Edit: I forgot one. <br /> Royal Door: Couldn't decide between Craft: Fortifications and Rage until he realized Rage wasn't a skill. Did I say Rage? I meant Integrity. Which he bought fully but already had a Defining Intimacy that Changing My Mind Is Wrong. Has a 3 dot artifact mustache. Took the Ptesence Specialty: Adornable. Divided his armies into &quot;Boring But Practical&quot; and &quot;Fanatic Zealots (even by our standards)&quot;. Couldn't figure out how to get the Prussian Troops high drill thing across so he basically dropped it. His Zealot army took beastman stats but are in-game humans. They benefit from Salty Dog and Sea Devil training despite not being sailors. When the Practical army doesnt have direct orders, they reinforce their base. They have craft: fortifications 5 and Specialty: Fortifying. Despite this they are on Offense 95% of the time. <br /> <br /> *&amp;$)\u00f7\u00a5 and #\u00a5\u00d7%\u2606%: the Sidereals assure me there is nothing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":8830,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","user":"Sorcerous Overlord","date":". 06-03-2020, 07:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T07:35:22-07:00","id":1393626,"title":"","content":"What about the Necrons, Tau, Orkz, Eldar, Dark Eldar, and Tyranids?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T21:23:31-07:00","id":1393737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1393626#post1393626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the Necrons, Tau, Orkz, Eldar, Dark Eldar, and Tyranids?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oof. Ok. <br /> <br /> Necrons- The Silent King is the actual First-Ever Zenith. Has Influence 5 and Backing 5, oversaw the first High Tech empire. However, he wasn't able to fix his people's extremely short lifespans so he made a pact with Autobot to live forever. It went horribly right. Sidenote: his units are considered to each wear Heavy Artifact Armor and they invented Flamepieces. Currently look down on Alchemicals as posers. They have an entire fleet of Flying Manses, and the Manse is able to cast Death Ray. <br /> <br /> Orks- took the Lunar rules for abilities but the Fae rules for social desires so now they only care about Bein Swole and War. They have a charm that let's them use any artifacts they find. They took a modified version of Peach of Immortality to grow new Orkz instead. They have a defining principle of &quot;Red Vehicles are faster than other colors&quot;. They can do Sorcerous Workings as a battlegroup even without sorcerers. <br /> <br /> Eldar- claim to be the Fair Folk. <br /> <br /> Dark Eldar- are the Actual Fair Folk <br /> <br /> Tyranids- took the Lunar chimera tree and maxed it out. Tied their tell to carapace and took unusual hide at max rank. The ST let them take artifact swords and scythes and tie it to their war form. After taking Craft: Bioengineering 5 they were able to make self replenishing size 5 bgs with poor drill. They have a defining principle of Absorb The Strong, Discard the Weak<br /> They invented the thousand streams river project. <br /> <br /> Tau- they are a new species that Gaia made in seclusion and didnt want the others to find. Theyre led by the Exigent of Technological Progression and they have a Defining Principle of Self Sacrifice for the Greater Good. Alchemicals do not like this at all. They were all made with the Spiritually Incorruptable merit, which prevents Demons and Spirits from even attempting Social Influence on them, and is a perfect defense against Demonic Social Charms. They are able to make, and design, new Warstriders. They are actually surprised no one else does. <br /> <br /> Tech Priests of Mars- Cthonians who wish they were Alchemicals<br /> <br /> Men of Iron- Alchemicals who wish they were Cthonians. <br /> <br /> Chaos Gods- 4 primordials who think they are infathomable eldritch horrors. They are just regular eldritch horrors though. <br /> <br /> Chaos Faction - Malfean humans. <br /> <br /> Space Marines- Deebs who think they are Solars<br /> <br /> Chaos Space Marines- Deebs who think they are Infernals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T07:38:47-07:00","id":1393778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1393737#post1393737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Chaos Gods- 4 primordials who think they are infathomable eldritch horrors. They are just regular eldritch horrors though.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That did make me chuckle, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T03:36:10-07:00","id":1394532,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> I was just rewatching some episodesof She ra, and think I get what the sword did in Exalted terms. The way I'm seeing it, it seems the sword had a custom evocation that acts as a Solar version of Deadly Beastman Transformation. That's why she grew to 8ft tall, had all her attributes jacked, and appeared more radiantly awesome. And when the daiklaive broke, she then learned a version of Glorious Solar Saber and created a similar evocation with the sword that gave her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-07T08:28:06-07:00","id":1394776,"title":"","content":"<u><b>DC Comics Classics:</b></u> (<i>I did these in 2.5e style, because that's what I'm most familiar with, to give them the best Exalted approximations I could come up with.</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>Superman -</b> Zenith Caste Solar specializing in MA, with Arms of the Unconquered Sun and Solar Hero Charms. Equipped with orichalcum Wings of the Raptor cloak and a Jewel of the Burning Gaze set in its clasp, plus hearthstone bracers set with a Gem of Adamant Skin. Bond-mate with Wonder Woman.<br /> <br /> <b>Wonder Woman -</b> Full Moon Lunar (eagle spirit shape) with moonsilver daiklave and thunderbolt shield, and orichalcum dire chain, plus moonsilver hearthstone bracers and Dragon-tear tiara set with Gem of Immortality and Freedom Stone respectively. Bond-mate with Superman.<br /> <br /> <b>Batman - </b>Night Caste Solar specializing in MA with Night Breeze, White Veil, Crystal Chameleon, and Ebon Shadow Charms. Equipped with silken armor clothing and soulsteel Wings of the Raptor cloak set with Precision of Form Gemstone, orichalcum chain daiklave set with Chameleon Stone, orichalcum skycutter, Gauntlet of Distant Claws, Amulet of Shadow Walking (belt-clasp, 4-dot version), and Heaven Glory Shroud. Bond-mate with Catwoman.<br /> <br /> <b>Catwoman - </b>Changing Moon Lunar (cat spirit shape, obviously) specializing in MA with Tiger and Laughing Wounds Charms. Equipped with silken armor, moonsilver dire lash, and moonsilver hearthstone bracers set with Jewel of Youthful Suppleness. Obviously knows Claws of the Silver Moon and lots of Charisma and Appearance Charms as well. Bond-mate with Batman.<br /> <br /> <b>Green Lantern - </b>Twilight Caste Solar Adamant Circle sorcerer, equipped with orichalcum Ring of Being and Discreet Essence Armor set with a Gem of Sorcery. Bond-mate with the Flash. (<i>Thought about making him a Defiler Caste GSP, especially so I could give him a green flame-firing hellwand or infernal cannon, but that didn't seem to fit the heroic pattern of GL. Maybe he could have a stolen one that he uses with Righteous Devil Charms....</i>)<br /> <br /> <b>The Flash -</b> Changing Moon Lunar (cheetah spirit shape) specializing in MA with Lunar Hero and Tiger Charms. Equipped with moonsilver Discreet Essence Armor set with a Gem of Perfect Mobility, and a crap-ton of Dexterity Charms. Bond-mate with Green Lantern.<br /> <br /> <b>Aquaman - </b>Dawn Caste Solar Person of the Sea with a siaka Familiar. Equipped with orichalcum breastplate and trident set with a Stone of Aquatic Prowess, which he uses with Melee and Black Tide MA Charms. Haven't really thought of an appropriate bond-mate for him...<br /> <br /> <b>Martian Manhanuter - </b>Mosok Dragon King (probably an awakened Sleeper), with mastery of both the Flowing Water and Shimmering Water Paths to simulate his density manipulation and shape-shifting powers, respectively. Equipped with a Necklace of Solar Charisma and a blue jade Wings of the Raptor cloak set with a Gemstone of Surface Thoughts.<br /> <br /> <b>Green Arrow -</b> Wood Aspect Dragon-Blood specializing in Wood Dragon MA (perhaps a former Immaculate), equipped with green jade powerbow set with a Kata-Sculpting Gem.<br /> <br /> <b>Cyborg - </b>Moonsilver Caste Alchemical specializing in MA with Live Wire and Thousand Wounds Gear Charms, and knowledge of Autochthonian thaumaturgy: Probabilistics (Master), Bioenhancement (Adept). Might need at least Man-Machine Protocol Weaving as well, to pull out some of Cyborg's more unpredicatable tricks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26206-sadric-of-ysyr","name":"Sadric of Ysyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26206_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T12:06:24-07:00","id":1406819,"title":"","content":"I've been thinking for a bit (read: two minutes) and I think, despite how obvious it seems to make him a Slayer Caste (haha), that Doomguy/the Doomslayer would be a Resistance Supernal Zenith. My reasonings:<br /> <br /> -Doomguy absolutely hates and I really mean HATES demons which are pretty much creatures of darkness in his settings<br /> <br /> -His weapons despite often being mortal weapons are capable of grievously harming even extremely tough demons, as if he were using charms that did aggravated damage on them<br /> <br /> -He is ridiculously tough. Like, able to take a shotgun to the face with little issue even in the original games where he had no helmet and just a standard-issue military combat vest. With armor he can take rockets and fireballs to the face. In addition, even when he's one step from death, he still can run and fight as well as he can at full health (yes, I know that that's just for gameplay purposes but hey, this thread's all about reading way too much into things)<br /> <br /> 2016 and Eternal throw a slight wrench into things but he took some Brawl charms (glory kills) and now wears an artifact Helltech suit with a built-in function that can generate healing and ammunition from sheer physicalized carnage (+ a chainklave for his chainsaw). He uses Firearms charms to never have to reload or reach for ammunition (he's not Firearms Supernal because he never does anything super fancy or blatantly supernatural with them besides hitting very hard,doing aggravated damage against demons/creatures of darkness). Finally, he has Athletics charms for his ridiculously fast run and his aerial maneuvers in the later games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-07T13:25:12-07:00","id":1406831,"title":"","content":"So I can be corrected if I'm seriously misreading something here, but...<br /> <br /> I've been playing a bunch of the Hitman games recently, and maybe it's just me, but Agent 47 really feels like a Chosen of Endings.<br /> <br /> His job is to take down important people for a nebulous, quasi-governmental agency which has some level of benefit to the status quo, but isn't afraid to change things when necessary. Or at least, its agents aren't.<br /> <br /> His MO is acquiring and using paper-thin disguises that people don't look at too hard because they see the uniform more than the person. That's a really natural evolution of Name-Pilfering Practice - taking someone else's entire destiny as a quick-change Resplendent Destiny. And he's always like steps within reach of making things &quot;coincidentally&quot; become a &quot;fatal accident.&quot;<br /> <br /> He really tries to avoid direct combat, but if he had like, a &quot;Pragmatism&quot; or &quot;Accidents&quot; SMA that would be really neat. Either way he's an undisputed master of improvised weapons.<br /> <br /> Diana is likely a Chosen of Secrets given how she interacts with him as a fellow member of ICA and his mission control.<br /> <br /> (Dunno exactly what I'd want to do with Lucas Grey and Olivia Hall - I was thinking a Day Caste Abyssal for Lucas and whether Olivia is exalted isn't super important, though I could see her being a Twilight or a No Moon pretty easily.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4500-kuiperbelt","name":"KuiperBelt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4500_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-10T21:56:30-07:00","id":1407444,"title":"","content":"I like to think that Orks are a strange fungal infection that came from the wyld, a combo of desires of war intermixing with plants and their desire to spread seeds and sprout in new places. They're basically like gigantic, rampaging moulds that can use their innate magic to create warstriders out of tree trunks and scrap metal, and get bigger and stronger the more fights they win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T04:48:31-07:00","id":1407675,"title":"","content":"Not sure I'd call that an orc, but that sounds like a fun concept for an antagonist group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T05:11:04-07:00","id":1407682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1407675#post1407675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure I'd call that an orc, but that sounds like a fun concept for an antagonist group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Accelerator is referring to WH40K Orkz, which are\u2026 markedly different from the ones in your typical D&amp;D settings.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never brought them into my games, but Squigs <i>are</i> part of my Wyld headcanon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-12T05:24:59-07:00","id":1407687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1389582-what-would-x-be-in-the-exalted-setting-redux?p=1407675#post1407675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure I'd call that an orc, but that sounds like a fun concept for an antagonist group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant wh40k ork. <br /> <br /> I mean, if you're not familiar, I can introduce you to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}